<title>COLOMBIA: Electronic Data Systems wins Colombian contract.</title>
<headline>Electronic Data Systems wins Colombian contract.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electronic Data Systems of the United States has won a $6.3 million service contract with Aerolineas Centrales de Colombia (ACES), Colombia's second biggest airline, ACES said.</p>
<p>It said the contract provided, among other services, for the installation of a computer system known as Lisline that would facilitate the programming of flights and crew movements.</p>
<p>((-- Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
